  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-sectoral Integrated Nutrition Action for Children, Adolescents and Women in Northeast Nigeria (MINA) II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MINA Phase II aligns with the purpose and scope of Phase I. This programme will address the food and nutrition security challenges and improve nutrition outcomes in children, adolescents and women in Northeast (NE) Nigeria through a gender transformative, inclusive, multi-sectoral response that builds the resilience of communities and systems to respond to multiple shocks. 
The MINA programme will complement FCDO&#x2019;s strategy to deliver life-saving humanitarian work by prioritizing the most vulnerable, protecting the most at-risk, preventing and anticipating future shocks, and building resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
